  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "While using FBT with hand tracking, turning your physical body in your playspace and trying to pinch to turn with your right hand, the orientation of the turn indicator will be locked to the direction you were originally standing in rather than the direction you are currently facing. As in, if you were to physically turn 90° to the right, then try pinching to turn, you will need to pinch forwards to turn right and pinch backwards to turn left. \n\nThis seems to be the same issue that [causes animations to trigger facing the wrong direction](https://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/1354-animations-face-the-wrong-direction), [causes objects that are direct children of the root of the avatar to get stuck in place rather than follow where you are looking](https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/bugdifferent-rotation-of-objects-not-in-armature-while-using-fbt), [breaks the AngularY parameter](https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/angulary-only-updates-during-locomotion-with-fbt-enabled), and causes scripts in worlds that rely on continuous teleports based on facing direction (e.g. climbing prefabs or swimming) to break.",
